  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0e80ae96b3eb9177eea5c8f9dadbcda1, type: 3}
  m_Name: MahoragaTerminalNode
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  displayText: "MAHORAGA\n\nSigurd's danger level: 95%\n\nScientific name: Makora
    Sila-Octo\nClassification: Uncontained Apex Anomaly\nObserved stature: ~3.75m
    (1.5x standard crew height)\n\nAn extremely tall, pale humanoid entity encountered\nacross
    abandoned Company facilities on all surveyed\nmoons. Despite possessing no eyes
    -- four rigid white\nwings erupt directly from its orbital sockets -- it\ntracks
    personnel through dark corridors with terrifying\nprecision and reacts violently
    to sound.\n\nA heavy blade is bound directly to its right forearm,\nand an ornate,
    eight-handled golden wheel hovers\nunsupported behind its skull.\n\nACOUSTIC
    WARNING:\nPersonnel consistently report an unmistakable low\nrhythmic pulse echoing
    through facility bulkheads well\nbefore visual contact. If the tone sharpens
    and loses\nits muffled quality, Mahoraga has line of sight.\n\nTHE WHEEL OF ADAPTATION:\nDo
    NOT rely on a single defense mechanism. Field black-\nbox recordings confirm
    that after enduring repeated\nstrikes or electrical/flash stuns of the same type,
    the\nfloating golden wheel turns 45 degrees with a loud\nmetallic chime. Upon
    each turn, the entity rapidly\nregenerates tissue and becomes nearly impervious
    to\nthat weapon or stun category for the remainder of the\nshift.\n\nSURVIVAL
    ADVISORY:\n- Standard locked doors will NOT stop it; it will force\n  them open
    within seconds.\n- Powered steel Blast Doors controlled from the ship\n  terminal
    CAN delay or isolate it. Coordinate with\n  your ship operator immediately.\n-
    Evacuation is strongly recommended. If termination is\n  attempted, crews must
    rotate diverse high-impact\n  weapons (firearms, explosives, melee) and deliver
    a\n  decisive lethal burst before the wheel completes its\n  turn.\n\n\"We hit
    it twice with the shotgun. The thing above its\nhead clicked like a giant clock,
    lit up gold, and the\nthird shell did nothing. Leave the scrap. Run.\"\n  --
    Recovered voice log, Moon 8-Titan"
  terminalEvent: 
